# Example. Copy into the repo and own it.
# bkit install does not write this file and does not overwrite a copy.

node_modules/
dist/
.agents/skills/
# Antigravity host installs as a workspace plugin; its skills/agents/hooks are
# force-overwritten renders like the other host mirrors below.
.agents/plugins/bkit/
# Canonical-overwrite content (byte-equal-text and markered-text entries of `getInstallManifest` in .bkit/core/engine/install/manifest.ts):
# bkit force-overwrites these on every install, so consumer prettier must not
# lint them. Width-sensitive rewrites would be reverted next install. The
# .opencode agent + command mirrors are force-overwritten just like .claude /
# .cursor (the managed-version marker and transform output are the source of
# truth, not a prettier rewrite). .opencode/plugin/ is listed for the same
# reason as .claude/ and .cursor/: its hook is a render of the template, and
# leaving it lintable would let prettier reformat the mirror but not the two ignored
# twins, silently diverging three copies that must stay byte-identical.
.claude/
.cursor/
.codex/
.opencode/agents/
.opencode/commands/
.opencode/plugin/
.github/
.husky/_/
*.tsbuildinfo
pnpm-lock.yaml
# bkit-written / reconciled files — bkit writes these with its own JSON.stringify
# layout (2-space, expanded arrays) and consumers have no prettier at install
# time, so prettier must not reformat them or the next install / `bkit check`
# would just revert the rewrite (permanent drift).
.mcp.json
.bkit/.env.example
.opencode/opencode.json
# Generated projection — `bkit roadmap fold` FULLY regenerates the
# `roadmap-status` marker block on every workflow close, emitting unpadded
# markdown tables. Prettier would re-pad them, so the committed board would
# never be byte-equal to what the renderer emits and every close would carry a
# formatting-only diff. The fold's output is the source of truth.
docs/roadmap.md
# Raw gate output — `bkit tests run` logs that workflows commit as `.md` beside
# a run's artifacts. The text is command output, not markdown; prettier would
# escape and reflow it, and a gate's own format check would fail on it.
docs/plans/*/logs/*/run-tests-*.md
docs/plans/*/logs/*/build-group-gate-*.md
docs/plans/*/logs/*/build-subplan-gate-*.md
docs/plans/*/logs/*/context-tests-local-*.md
# bkit's reference copies of its templates — refreshed by `bkit upgrade`, never
# formatted by this repo.
.bkit/templates/
